  "interpretation": {
    "limits": "Overlap categories describe box geometry after the fixed maximum-cardinality match. They do not inspect probability tensors, choose a new loss, or authorize a candidate.",
    "next_repair_hypothesis": "Isolate learned DB-mask boundary and extent supervision while holding the original BGR input, inverse targets, postprocessing, and operating point fixed. On validation, 32 of 43 misses overlap a prediction below IoU 0.5 and 35 of 47 extras overlap truth; the fixed perfect-target oracle reaches 181 of 183 truths. This supports an extent and split/merge repair hypothesis, not a proposal-threshold or postprocessor change.",
    "responsible_subsystems_are_separated": "A no-overlap miss means no emitted box overlaps the truth; probability-map and decoder rejection causes remain unresolved. Positive-overlap subthreshold misses describe extent/localization differences. Multi-truth and multi-prediction overlap describes possible merge/split behavior. These categories do not identify a specific loss-function defect. Role confusion uses the same geometry assignment.",
    "role_context_diagnosis": "The DB detector constructs OcrDetectedRegion without OcrRegionContext. OcrPipeline only infers AxisTitleExpected for tall text left of the plot. GraphTextRoleClassifier can emit Participant only from InParticipantBand or ExplicitRoleHint, neither of which this candidate path supplies. Therefore 0 of 39 participant truths being role-correct is an unavailable runtime-context path, not evidence that recognition text alone can learn the participant role. This diagnostic does not add a context rule."
  },
